1
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:13,556
Beside the games, the platform has awareness corners.

2
00:00:13,616 --> 00:00:22,063
Each corner explains a topic with short, sourced cards and makes you think with two activities.

3
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:32,203
Autism is a difference in how the brain develops; it can shape how a person perceives the world and communicates.

4
00:00:32,263 --> 00:00:40,368
Autistic people are in our classes, on our campus and among our neighbours.

5
00:00:41,078 --> 00:00:48,048
Down syndrome is not an illness but a genetic difference; every person is unique.

6
00:00:48,108 --> 00:00:56,639
Awareness starts with respectful language and a school where everyone takes part.

7
00:00:57,349 --> 00:01:04,239
Leukaemia is not contagious, and most childhood leukaemias can be treated today.

8
00:01:04,299 --> 00:01:10,876
A friend in treatment needs understanding and support most of all.

9
00:01:11,586 --> 00:01:18,556
Enough sleep, daily movement and balanced screen time are parts of a healthy day.

10
00:01:18,616 --> 00:01:25,114
A smoke-free space is good for everyone.

11
00:01:25,824 --> 00:01:30,644
11 November is National Tree Planting Day in Türkiye.

12
00:01:30,704 --> 00:01:39,351
Trees give oxygen, protect the soil and are home to many living things.

13
00:01:40,061 --> 00:01:48,031
Exiled from their homeland in 1944, the Ahıska Turks kept their language and traditions alive.

14
00:01:48,091 --> 00:01:55,622
The corner tells this story with age-appropriate, sourced cards.

15
00:01:56,332 --> 00:02:03,922
The remembrance and empathy corners use age-appropriate, respectful and sourced language.

16
00:02:03,982 --> 00:02:11,893
No people is blamed as a whole; the aim is to understand and to remember.

17
00:02:12,603 --> 00:02:20,493
Every corner has sourced cards and two activities: “True or false?” and “What would you do?”.

18
00:02:20,553 --> 00:02:28,165
The writing is short, age-appropriate and puts people first.

